     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h1_1:pivot and h2_1:pivot makes crown:obtain unreachable. One block is not enough, because two attack paths share no blockable step: edge0 -> h2_1 -> h3_2 -> h5_2 -> crown, and edge0 -> h1_1 -> h3_1 -> h5_0 -> crown. Blocking h1_1 cuts h3_1 and the AND step h3_0, so h5_1, h4_0 and h3_0's route into h4_2 all fail. Blocking h2_1 cuts h3_2 (and so h5_2) and h2_1's route into h4_2. With h4_0, h4_2 and h3_1 all unreachable, h5_0 also fails, so every parent of crown is unreachable.\"}"
